<title>JAPAN: Japan MOF plans to auction 2-year notes on Friday.</title>
<headline>Japan MOF plans to auction 2-year notes on Friday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance (MOF) plans to offer two-year government notes through a price-competitive auction on Friday, a MOF official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The volume of the offer is likely to be 120 billion yen and the coupon rate 0.8 percent, traders said.</p>
<p>When MOF last auctioned two-year notes on June 26, it offered 120 billion yen of 1.0 percent two-year notes.</p>
</text>
